# Journal logs for setting up Flora infrastructures
## Prepare base openSUSE Leap 16
Follow homogeneous setup with same base OS for all machines, converging toward same state (wishful thinking, that's not gonna happen).
### Flash OS with Online installer
- For local machine, use https://get.opensuse.org/leap/16.0/#download
- For HostHatch VM, use "Upload ISO" and paste this link, then follow the same procedure like local: https://mirror.freedif.org/opensuse/distribution/leap/16.0/offline/Leap-16.0-online-installer-x86_64-Build178.27.install.iso
### Setup SSH connectivity and enroll machine into Tailnet
- Execute `sudo systemctl enable --now sshd` on target machine
- Create and add the keys into the nodes
```bash
ssh-keygen ed25519 -C "localflora-shared" -f ~/.ssh/localflora-shared-ed25519
ssh-keygen ed25519 -C "exoticflora-shared" -f ~/.ssh/exoticflora-shared-ed25519
ssh-copy-id -i ~/.ssh/localflora-shared-ed25519 login-user@target-address
ssh-copy-id -i ~/.ssh/exoticflora-shared-ed25519 login-user@target-address
```
- Go to Tailscale, create auth-key for unattended Tailscale node enrollment = X-Key
- Install tailscale, enable systemd service and enroll
```bash
sudo zypper install -y tailscale
sudo systemctl enable --now tailscaled
sudo tailscale up --auth-key=X-Key
```
### Disable SSH-via-password
- SSH to node, add disable SSH-via-password config
```
sudo tee /etc/ssh/sshd_config.d/disable-password.conf <<EOF
PasswordAuthentication no
ChallengeResponseAuthentication no
UsePAM no
EOF
```
- Execute `sudo systemctl restart sshd`
### Setup Firewall rules
- Allow Tailscale traffics in `internal` zone (LAN-ish zone)
```bash
sudo firewall-cmd --permanent --zone=internal --add-interface=tailscale0
sudo firewall-cmd --permanent --zone=internal --add-service=ssh
sudo firewall-cmd --permanent --zone=internal --add-service=cockpit
sudo firewall-cmd --permanent --zone=internal --add-service=mdns
sudo firewall-cmd --permanent --zone=internal --add-service=dhcpv6-client
sudo firewall-cmd --permanent --zone=internal --add-service=samba-client
```
- Drop `public` zone traffic by removing services
```bash
sudo firewall-cmd --permanent --zone=public --remove-service=ssh
sudo firewall-cmd --permanent --zone=public --remove-service=cockpit
sudo firewall-cmd --permanent --zone=public --remove-service=samba-client
sudo firewall-cmd --permanent --zone=public --remove-service=dhcpv6-client
sudo firewall-cmd --permanent --zone=public --set-target=DROP
```
- (optional, for local) Leave some services on for `public` zone (DO NOT REMOVE `mdns`)
```bash
sudo firewall-cmd --permanent --zone=public --add-service=cockpit
```
- Apply rules with `sudo firewall-cmd --reload`
### Disable swap
- Comment out the swap entry in `/etc/fstab` to prevent enabling swap in after next reboot.
- Check `sudo systemctl list-units --type=swap`, and mask the systemd unit
```bash
sudo systemctl mask <unit>.swap
sudo swapoff -a
sudo reboot
```

- Verify using `free -h` to see if swap = 0GB
### Load kernel modules
- Create a configuration file defining what to load for k8s-specific requirements
```bash
sudo tee /etc/modules-load.d/k8s.conf <<EOF
overlay
br_netfilter
EOF
```
- Load config immediately
```bash
sudo modprobe overlay
sudo modprobe br_netfilter
```
- Check with `sudo lsmod | grep "overlay|br_netfilter"`
- (optional) Reboot
### Tune kernel parameters
- Add these (who knows what they are about lol), then apply
```bash
sudo tee /etc/sysctl.d/k8s.conf <<EOF
net.bridge.bridge-nf-call-iptables  = 1
net.bridge.bridge-nf-call-ip6tables = 1
net.ipv4.ip_forward                 = 1
EOF
sudo sysctl --system
```
- Verify
```bash
sysctl net.bridge.bridge-nf-call-iptables net.bridge.bridge-nf-call-ip6tables net.ipv4.ip_forward
```
